# Architecture Details

## Layers

### Composition Root (App)
- Read launch options, init global services/configs/save/dev tools, create player, start/stop `RaidSession`, handle scene transitions, attach IMGUI overlays and presenters.
- `App.Instance` allowed only here.

**Bootstrap flow** (`AppBootstrap.cs`, `[DefaultExecutionOrder(1000)]`):
1. `Awake`: guard against double-init, `App.Initialize()`, `DontDestroyOnLoad`, attach overlays (HotbarDebugOverlay, InventoryUI, QuestUI, AimCursorOverlay, DamageNumberOverlay, StatusEffectOverlay, CraftingUI, StaminaBarOverlay, DefenderArmorHUD, DeployUI, NpcUI)
2. `Start`: build `LaunchOptions` from inspector `_launchMode`, call `GameLauncher.Launch(options)`
3. `Update` → `App.Instance.Tick()`, `LateUpdate` → `App.Instance.LateTick()`

**App singleton**: owns adapters (5), presenters (7), `Player`, `RaidSession`, `QuestDatabase`.
**Presenters** (ticked in `LateTick`): Destructible, Player, Bot, Projectile, Grenade, GroundItem, Corpse.

### Session Layer
- `Player`: persistent profile, meta progression, save/load entry point.
- `RaidSession`: owns `RaidState`/`LevelState`, constructs `RaidContext`, orchestrates system execution in stable order, manages hit/collision inboxes, handles interaction dispatch, processes damage alerts and death events.

### Domain Logic (Systems)
- Stateless static functions operating on explicit state and context.
- Accept inputs as arguments, mutate state via `ref`.
- Must not depend on hidden globals.

### Adapters (Ports)
All Unity subsystem access through interfaces passed via context:
- `ITimeAdapter` → `UnityTimeAdapter` (DeltaTime, FixedDeltaTime, Time)
- `IInputAdapter` → `UnityInputAdapter` (move, aim, hotbar, ADS, convergence, muzzle)
- `INavMeshAdapter` → `UnityNavMeshAdapter` (SamplePosition)
- `IPhysicsAdapter` → `UnityPhysicsAdapter` (Linecast)
- `IGrenadePositionAdapter` → `GrenadePositionAdapter` (grenade world position by EId)
- `IRaidEvents` → `RaidEventBuffer` (31 event types)

### View / Presenter
- Translates state and domain events into transforms, animation, VFX, SFX, UI.
- Must not make gameplay decisions.

## Data flow

### State buckets
- `PlayerProfileState` (persistent), `RaidState` (per run), `LevelState` (per level/run).
- Values and IDs only. No Unity object references.

**RaidState fields**: ElapsedTime, IsRunning, PlayerEntity, Projectiles, Grenades, HealthMap, GroundItems, Bots, Lootables, Workbenches, DeployPoints, Npcs, Inventory, StatusEffects, ArmorMap.

### Context (`RaidContext`)
- Readonly struct passed as `in`.
- Contains: DeltaTime, Events (IRaidEvents), Time, Input, NavMesh, Physics, GrenadePositions, AimConfig, ShootingConfig.
- `AimConfig`: aim split, follow multipliers, recoil recovery (from DevCheats).
- `ShootingConfig`: parallax, convergence, speed/damage multipliers, recoil, infinite ammo (from DevCheats).

### Events
- Systems emit domain-to-view intents through `IRaidEvents`.
- `RaidEventBuffer` stores events as `List<RaidEvent>` (struct with enum + flat payload). Zero-alloc after warm-up.
- Presenter iterates `buffer.All`, filters by `RaidEventType`.
- **31 event types**: RaidStarted/Ended, PlayerSpawned, Projectile(Spawned/Despawned/Hit), Entity(Damaged/Died), GroundItem(Spawned/Despawned), Bot(Spawned/Despawned), Weapon(Fired/EquipStarted/UnequipStarted/EquipFinished/ReloadStarted/ReloadFinished/DryFired), Grenade(Spawned/Exploded/Despawned), Medkit(UseStarted/UseStopped), HitConfirmed, StatusEffect(Applied/Removed), Lootable(Spawned/Despawned), DamageNumber, ArmorBroken, ProjectileRicochet.

## Tick model
1. Gather input and external signals.
2. Run systems in deterministic order.
3. Produce state changes and domain events.
4. Present state and events in Unity.

Actual system tick order in `RaidSession.Tick()`:
```
// Pre-movement
ADS state + blend (inline)       // before movement so speed is affected this frame
StaminaSystem                    // sprint drain/regen, stamina gate
RollSystem                       // dodge roll state machine
MovementSystem                   // player locomotion

// Weapon pipeline
WeaponSyncSystem                 // syncs weapon state from inventory/equipment
WeaponEquipSystem                // writes PendingHotbarSlot (intent only)
WeaponStateMachineSystem         // FSM: Ready/Firing/Cooldown/Equipping/Unequipping/Reloading
AimingSystem                     // dual-layer: RawAimPoint → WeaponAimPoint → AimDirection

// Consumables + status effects
QuickSlotSystem                  // quick slot usage
GrenadeSystem                    // grenade throw + trajectory
MedkitSystem                     // healing consumable
StatusEffectSystem               // bleed L1/L2, buffs
BandageSystem                    // bandage healing

// Combat
ShootingSystem                   // fires only when Phase == Ready; ammo gate + dry fire + auto-reload

// AI
PlayerFOVSystem                  // visibility cone queries
BotPerceptionSystem
BotBrainSystem
BotMovementSystem
BotCombatSystem                  // bots use LastFireTime, no FSM

// Resolution
ProjectileSystem
GrenadeSystem.TickExplosions     // grenade detonation + area damage
DamageSystem                     // consumes hit inbox, armor calc, applies damage, emits death events
ProcessCollisions / ProcessDamageAlerts / ProcessDeathEvents
Interaction dispatch (inline)    // NPC / Deploy / Craft / Loot / GroundItem pickup
ElapsedTime += dt
```

## Entry points
Supported via `LaunchMode` enum: Menu, Raid, TestScenario, Hideout.
All go through `GameLauncher.Launch(LaunchOptions)`. Do not rely on directly loading arbitrary scenes.

## Debug tools

### Raid State Debugger (EditorWindow)
- `Assets/Scripts/Editor/RaidStateDebuggerWindow.cs`
- Opens via **Window → Raid State Debugger**
- Readonly view of entire `RaidState` updated every frame during Play Mode
- Shows: Player, Bots, Projectiles, Ground Items, Inventory, Health Map, Status Effects, Armor Map, Workbenches, Deploy Points, NPCs, Lootables
- **Rule**: when adding new fields to any state class, add corresponding display in the debugger window

### Dev Cheats (EditorWindow + ScriptableObject)
- `Assets/Scripts/Editor/DevCheatsWindow.cs` — **Window → Dev Cheats**
- SO-based: `DevCheats.cs` (static accessor) → `DevCheatsConfig.cs` (root SO) → 14 section SOs
- Sections: Cheats, Weapon, Recoil, Aim, Player, FOV, Fog, Crosshair, ADS, HealthBar, Parallax, DamageNumbers, StatusEffects, Armor

### Bot BT Debugger
- `Assets/Scripts/Editor/BotBTDebuggerWindow.cs` — behavior tree visualization

### Quest Editor Tools
- `Assets/Scripts/Editor/Quests/` — QuestDefinitionEditor, QuestGraphImporter, QuestPrerequisiteGraph, QuestNode

### Raid Tools Menu
- **Raid → Delete Save** — clears save file

### Other debug tools
- `HotbarDebugOverlay` — IMGUI: 9 hotbar slots with mag/reserve ammo
- `BotDebugLabel` — 3D TextMesh: TypeId, AI status, HP, distance
- `InventoryUI` — IMGUI: inventory screen with drag/drop, context menu, stack counts, item tooltip
- `GrenadeTrajectoryOverlay` — grenade throw preview arc

## Data Flow Reference

### Tick lifecycle

```
Update
  └─ App.Tick()
       └─ RaidSession.Tick()
            ├─ build RaidContext (readonly struct, AimConfig + ShootingConfig from DevCheats)
            ├─ ADS state + blend (inline)
            ├─ StaminaSystem → RollSystem → MovementSystem → ...
            ├─ ... (all systems in deterministic order, see tick model)
            ├─ DamageSystem → ProcessCollisions → ProcessDamageAlerts → ProcessDeathEvents
            ├─ Interaction dispatch (inline)
            └─ state.ElapsedTime += dt

LateUpdate
  └─ App.LateTick()
       ├─ DestructiblePresenter → PlayerPresenter → BotPresenter → ProjectilePresenter
       ├─ GrenadePresenter → GroundItemPresenter → CorpsePresenter
       └─ RaidSession.ClearEvents()
```

### Object ownership

```
App (singleton, composition root)
  ├─ Adapters (5 interfaces, 5 implementations)
  ├─ Presenters (7 plain C# classes, ticked + disposed by App)
  ├─ Player (persistent profile + inventory)
  ├─ QuestDatabase (SO from Resources)
  └─ RaidSession (created per raid)
       ├─ RaidEventBuffer (IRaidEvents)
       ├─ HitInbox / CollisionInbox
       ├─ RaidState (entities, health, armor, status effects, inventory, etc.)
       └─ LevelState (level metadata)
```

### Data direction

```
Input → Adapter → Context → System → State → Presenter → View
                                ↓
                          EventBuffer → Presenter (spawn/destroy intents)
```

No reverse links. State does not know about View.
Systems do not know about App. View does not write into State.
